> #3.10)	fi'a do dunda fe le vi rozgu
> #	[what place]? you give x2= the nearby rose
> #	Are you the giver or the receiver of this rose?
> 
> Interesting question: what would "fi'a do dunda le rozgu" mean? Your using
> "fe" implies to me that it'd depend on the answer: the rose would be either
> x2 or x4. And yet thinking that it would still be x2 would come naturally
> to me. I think you need to flesh this out more, that the sentence really
> takes on meaning only when the blank of "fi'a" is filled in.

No, "le vi rozgu" is necessarily x2 if untagged, because there have been
no actual numeric tags ("fi'a" doesn't count), and it is the first place
after the selbri.  I'll rewrite so as to clarify these points.

